      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Research in Congo</strong><br>\nIn 1966, Fossey began her research in the Congo, establishing a research center she named \"Karisoke\" in the Virunga Mountains. Her focus was to study the behavior and social interactions of mountain gorillas. The political instability and civil war in Congo, however, forced her to leave the country shortly after she started her work.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Relocation to Rwanda</strong><br>\nFossey relocated to Rwanda, where she resumed her work and spent most of her life studying the mountain gorillas. She lived in a remote mountain cabin and often faced challenging conditions. Her dedication led to new insights into the family and social life of gorillas, including their hierarchical structure and communal relationships.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Advocacy for Gorillas</strong><br>\nFossey became a staunch advocate for the conservation of mountain gorillas. She opposed poaching and the capture of gorillas for zoos, often confronting poachers and advocating for anti-poaching laws. Fossey's active conservation efforts led to significant tension with local authorities and poaching communities.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
