          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>\"Gorillas in the Mist\"</strong><br>\nTo raise awareness about the plight of the mountain gorillas, Fossey wrote \"Gorillas in the Mist.\" Published in 1983, the book is a detailed account of her research and the daily lives of the gorillas. It became an international bestseller and was later adapted into a feature film, which helped to popularize Fossey's conservation efforts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Challenges and Controversies</strong><br>\nFossey's methods of conservation and her direct confrontations with poachers were controversial. She was often criticized for her extreme tactics, which some considered to be anti-social and overly aggressive. Despite criticism, she maintained her methods were necessary for the survival of the gorillas.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mysterious Death</strong><br>\nOn December 26, 1985, Dian Fossey was found murdered in her cabin in Rwanda. The case remains unsolved, with various theories about her death related to her anti-poaching stance. Fossey's legacy lives on through the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund International, which continues her work in gorilla conservation and protection.</p>\n"
              },
